# PHPDoc (Laravel / PHP)

## Scope

| Area | PHPDoc required |
|------|-----------------|
| `app/Http/Controllers`, `app/Services`, `app/Models` | **File header** + class + public/protected/**private** methods |
| `app/Http/Requests`, `app/Enums`, `app/Exceptions` | **File header** + class (+ methods when non-trivial) |
| `features/bootstrap/` (Behat context) | **File header** + class + methods (including private helpers) |
| `routes/`, `bootstrap/`, `config/`, `database/factories/`, `database/seeders/`, `public/` | **File header** (one-sentence role of the file); named classes and methods when present |
| `tests/`, `database/migrations/` | No (Pest/Gherkin steps and schema files stay lean) |

## Content

- **File header** (top of file, after `<?php`): one English sentence describing what the file owns (routes, config keys, bootstrap wiring, etc.). Enforced by `Squiz.Commenting.FileComment` in PHPCS; empty blocks are rejected by `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.EmptyComment`. Compatible with Laravel Pint blank line after `<?php`.
- **Class/trait/enum doc**: implementation-focused summary; avoid repeating the file header verbatim.
- Description in **English**, one sentence (business or technical role) on classes and methods.
- **`@param`** for every parameter (short description after the name, per Squiz).
- **`@return`** on every method (use `void` when applicable).
- `@property` on Eloquent models when useful for PHPStan.
- No empty `//` placeholders in methods: use `{}` instead.

```php
<?php

/**
 * REST API route definitions for health, auth, QuickBooks OAuth, and time activities.
 */

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Route;
```

```php
/**
 * Creates a time activity in QuickBooks for the user's employee.
 */
public function createForUser(User $user, QuickBooksToken $token, array $validated): object
```

## Backend lint

| Tool | Role | Command |
|------|------|---------|
| **Pint** | Laravel style | `composer format:check` |
| **PHPCS** + Slevomat | Required PHPDoc | `composer phpcs` |
| **PHP_CodeSniffer Community** (IDE) | Real-time PHPCS on save | Extension `phpcscommunity.php-codesniffer` |
| **PHPStan 5** + Larastan | Static analysis | `composer analyse` |
| **Pest Arch** | Structure (QBO SDK only in services) | `composer test:arch` |

PHPCS config: `backend/phpcs.xml`. Aggregate: `composer lint` (= Pint + PHPCS).

## Agent routine

1. New class or method in PHPCS scope (`backend/phpcs.xml`): PHPDoc before finishing.
2. `cd backend && composer lint && composer analyse && composer test`.
3. QuickBooks SDK: only in `app/Services/` (plus token conversion on the model).
